WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.396
Reliance is built to help customers understand what happened during a service without guessing.

00:00:05.416 --> 00:00:07.602
Start with the service record.

00:00:07.622 --> 00:00:14.796
This is where Reliance shows the current state of the work, the public service video status, and whether a review is available.

00:00:14.816 --> 00:00:18.264
Service videos are short approved stage previews.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.776
They are not full-job recordings.

00:00:20.796 --> 00:00:27.933
They help customers see the starting condition, the work in progress, and the final result when those clips are available.

00:00:27.953 --> 00:00:31.597
Customer reviews and Reliance Trust Score are separate.

00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:35.997
A customer review is feedback from the person who received the service.

00:00:36.017 --> 00:00:39.881
The Trust Score is based on verified platform activity.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:44.122
If a video is not available yet, Reliance should explain why.

00:00:44.142 --> 00:00:50.494
It may still need approval, access may not be granted, or the final-result clip may not exist yet.

00:00:50.514 --> 00:00:53.901
When in doubt, open the service record first.

00:00:53.921 --> 00:00:58.725
It should tell you what is complete, what is waiting, and what you can do next.
